{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/postgres","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:08.012Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/postgres/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/postgres/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Postgres image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is PostgreSQL?\n\nPostgreSQL, often simply \"Postgres\", is an object-relational database management system (ORDBMS) with an emphasis on extensibility and standards-compliance. As a database server, its primary function is to store data, securely and supporting best practices, and retrieve it later, as requested by other software applications, be it those on the same computer or those running on another computer across a network (including the Internet). It can handle workloads ranging from small single-machine applications to large Internet-facing applications with many concurrent users. Recent versions also provide replication of the database itself for security and scalability.\n\nPostgreSQL implements the majority of the SQL:2011 standard, is ACID-compliant and transactional (including most DDL statements) avoiding locking issues using multiversion concurrency control (MVCC), provides immunity to dirty reads and full serializability; handles complex SQL queries using many indexing methods that are not available in other databases; has updateable views and materialized views, triggers, foreign keys; supports functions and stored procedures, and other expandability, and has a large number of extensions written by third parties. In addition to the possibility of working with the major proprietary and open source databases, PostgreSQL supports migration from them, by its extensive standard SQL support and available migration tools. And if proprietary extensions had been used, by its extensibility that can emulate many through some built-in and third-party open source compatibility extensions, such as for Oracle.\n\nSee: [wikipedia.org/wiki/PostgreSQL](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PostgreSQL)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `16`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to postgresql version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Start a Postgres instance\n\n    docker run --name postgres-server -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=secret -d -p 49153:5432 mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/postgres:16\n\n\nThe default postgres user and database are created in the entrypoint with initdb.\n\nThe postgres database is a default database meant for use by users, utilities and third party applications.\nSee: [postgresql.org/docs](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/app-initdb.html).\n\nThe default container startup command is `postgres`.\n\n### Launch Azure Linux shell\n\nThe Postgres image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to Launch Azure Linux shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/postgres:16 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-12T02:11:37.724548+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"40K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"16","digest":"sha256:704bb1636af09043b9fc4ae49b33188d6429405b87d28d227953152730f4db79","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:27:28.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"16.15-1-azl3.0.20260909","digest":"sha256:704bb1636af09043b9fc4ae49b33188d6429405b87d28d227953152730f4db79","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:27:21.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"16.15-1-azl3.0.20260909-arm64","digest":"sha256:772a0ea612649b7a2bff6678fb62196a8844bbecb0696de632937e60ab900579","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:27:20.0000000+00:00","size":5848,"platforms":["linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"16.15-1-azl3.0.20260909-amd64","digest":"sha256:580b0524e90781e1e84db8c54c57d883e4dddfdaa1b5d1b7b1896ce0ac43cbc2","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:27:12.0000000+00:00","size":5859,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"16.15-1-azl3.0.20260825","digest":"sha256:cd409d293e8055932128ed70f90ff789d2cff3a53699ea464c08615844e04497","pushed":"2026-08-26T01:30:07.000